The '''2026 Kirklees Metropolitan Borough Council election''' will take place on 7 May 2026 alongside [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]]. All 69 seats of [[Kirklees Metropolitan Borough Council]] will be elected.<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 2025 |others=Kirklees Council |title=Scheduled elections |url=https://www.kirklees.gov.uk/beta/voting-and-elections/scheduled-elections.aspx |archive-url=http://web.archive.org/web/20250906140517/https://www.kirklees.gov.uk/beta/voting-and-elections/scheduled-elections.aspx |archive-date=2025-09-06 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=www.kirklees.gov.uk |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In [[2024 Kirklees Metropolitan Borough Council election|2024]], Labour retained control of the council.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McCormick |first=Sebastian |date=2024-05-02 |title=Kirklees local election results 2024 in full |url=https://www.examinerlive.co.uk/news/local-news/kirklees-local-election-results-2024-29093598 |access-date=2026-01-27 |website=Yorkshire Live |language=en}}</ref> Due to defections, Labour lost control of the council mid-term and govern the council as a minority going into the 2026 election.

