Changes 2024–2026:
*May 2024: Masood Ahmed, Yusra Hussain, Mus Khan, Paul Moore, Cathy Scott, Adam Zaman, and Habiban Zaman (Labour) leave party to sit as independents<ref>{{cite web |last1=Boothroyd |first1=David |title=Kirklees leader defection |url=https://www.localcouncils.co.uk/2024/05/kirklees-leader-defection/ |website=LocalCouncils.co.uk |access-date=29 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Dillon |first1=Gemma |title=Kirklees councillor Musarrat Khan quits Labour over party's 'moral direction' |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leeds-69002985 |access-date=29 January 2026 |work=BBC News |date=13 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Boothroyd |first1=David |title=Kingstanding still |url=https://www.localcouncils.co.uk/2024/05/kingstanding-still/ |website=LocalCouncils.co.uk |access-date=29 January 2026}}</ref>
*September 2024: [[Paul Davies (Labour politician)|Paul Davies]] (Labour) resigns – by-election held October 2024<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marlow |first1=Abigail |title=Kirklees councillor resigns to focus on new MP role |url=https://www.examinerlive.co.uk/news/west-yorkshire-news/kirklees-councillor-resigns-focus-new-29857878 |access-date=29 January 2026 |work=Yorkshire Live |date=3 September 2024 |language=en}}</ref>
*October 2024: Damian Brook (Conservative) gains by-election from Labour<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Holme Valley South Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/1381/#2024-10-17 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=29 January 2026}}</ref>
*January 2026: Community Alliance Kirklees formed – Masood Ahmed, Ammar Anwar, Yusra Hussain, Cathy Scott, Adam Zaman, and Habiban Zaman join party<ref>{{cite news |last1=Shaw |first1=Martin |title=Former Kirklees Council leader Cathy Scott's Community Alliance registered as official political party |url=https://huddersfieldhub.co.uk/former-kirklees-council-leader-cathy-scotts-community-alliance-registered-as-official-political-party/ |access-date=29 January 2026 |work=Huddersfield Hub |date=21 January 2026}}</ref>
*March 2026: The death of Cahal Burke (Liberal Democrats) caused a vacancy in Lindley ward<ref>{{Cite web |last=KLTV |date=2026-03-10 |title=Former Kirklees Mayor Cllr Cahal Burke dies aged 48 |url=https://kirkleeslocaltv.com/news/former-kirklees-mayor-cllr-cahal-burke-dies-aged-48/ |access-date=2026-03-10 |website=KLTV |language=en-GB}}</ref>

